==Battleground==
*20 [[Shibalien]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 7.33~8.67 seconds<sup>220f~260f</sup>.
*1 [[Spacefish Jones]] spawns as the boss after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*1 [[Corporal Weyland]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hyppoh]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*3 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*10 [[Shibalien]]s spawn after 103.33 seconds<sup>3,100f</sup>, delay 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shibalien]]s spawn after 110 seconds<sup>3,300f</sup>, delay 10~10.67 seconds<sup>300f~320f</sup>.
*5 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 110 seconds<sup>3,300f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Very easily rushable with only a few cats. As this stage falls apart if Spacefish Jones is removed, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] is enough to kill it in 1 cycle. There are only 3 Shibaliens shielding Spacefish Jones at the start and clearing these will allow Bahamut and Fishman to quickly dispose of Jones. Higher crowned difficulties make this strategy very difficult, thus the alternative below is preferred.

The main issue of this stage is buffed [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] protecting Spacefish Jones with crazy strong Zang Roos to dig under and reach your backliners. Not to mention that each Zang Roo has a staggering 24.7k DPS. With strong backliners slowly pushing after each Zang Roo, this stage becomes an endurance stage.

Two meatshields should be enough, but when the wave of Zang Roos arrive, you need [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] against the Zang Roos, like [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]] or [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]. It is also recommended to use [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] to unburrow the Zang Roos and quickly kill them before they become an overwhelming issue using units like [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] or [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver Bearcat]].

Alternatively you can exploit the Zang Roos' burrow to seperate them from the Aliens. However, this requires slipping a powerful [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien]] Tanker such as [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] to stall the Aliens for long enough for you to kill the Zang Roo before repeating the process for each Zang Roo.

Once the Zang Roo waves have been exhausted, your typical anti-Aliens like [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] can handle cleanup.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[EVA Unit-01 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-01]]: Strong vs. both Aliens and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] and helps out a lot with damage.
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]]: Massive Damage to Aliens and Long Distance attacks, may do lots of damage to Spacefish Jones.
*[[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]]: Lots of survivability with constant slow procs, definitely helps against the Zang Roos.
*[[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Sentinels]]: Good DPS against Zombies with freeze procs and high survivability. Their Soulstrike Talent can help with damaging the Zang Roos that were not Z-killed.
*[[Queen Reika (Uber Rare Cat)|Eternal Reika]] does massive damage to both Aliens and Zombies. Be careful with her though, as she doesn't exactly have the highest health.
*[[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]] helps tremendously here with barrier-breaking [[Wave Attack]]s and incredible resistance to Aliens, turning the stage (nearly) into a joke with a few zombie damagers. Beware that it will be crippled if it's in the Zang Roos' way, though.
*[[Doktor Heaven (Legend Rare Cat)|Doktor Heaven/Professor Abyss]]: Both forms can be good here. Her first form can be used to tank the Aliens and Gravolodon can be used to kill the enemies. Her 2nd form can be used to deal a lot of damage to the Aliens, and in this case, Gravolodon, despite mostly being used for resisting, can be an alright attacker here.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Can freeze and do good DPS against all enemies in this stage.
*[[Mighty Kristul Muu (Legend Rare Cat)|Mighty Kristul Muu]]: It stays behind the frontline, protects your base and can easy pick off the Zang Roos that burrow past your frontline units.
*[[Lumina (Legend Rare Cat)|Luminalia]]: Adhere to the Tank strategy, and this unit makes the entire stage free, even on 3-Crown.

==Trivia==
*Going along with the theme of meat and cooking in [[Rose-Colored Road]], the tongues are presumably speechless because they have been separated from the body and cooked.
*This is the only stage in [[Uncanny Legends]] to feature [[Hyppoh]].
*This stage is one of the only two Uncanny Legends stages to feature [[Shibalien]], with the other one being [[Ajillo Highlands]].

